WEBVTT

cue0021386
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Life really is, besides observing or keeping, really educating.

cue0021387
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Education really is, if you look in the Tora, as far as I can see, and this is why the question is,

cue0021388
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
the only places where they really tell you to is in the Shemaʿ.

cue0021389
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Alright.

cue0021390
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
I can recall.

cue0021391
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Alright.

cue0021392
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
In two parts it uses the word about teaching.

cue0021393
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Where else do they stress teaching?

cue0021394
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Alright.

cue0021395
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Now, you see, of course we were the people who invented the notion of education.

cue0021396
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Education, it's an unknown concept in antiquity, even in modern times.

cue0021397
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
For the Greeks, for instance, education is a matter of blood.

cue0021398
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
If you belong to the aristocracy, then you are educationable.

cue0021399
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
If you do not belong to the aristocracy, you cannot be educated.

cue0021400
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
In the same way that you cannot educate, I don't know, a rabbit or a pigeon or a cat,

cue0021401
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
you cannot educate somebody who is not from the aristocracy.

cue0021402
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
So, we were the ones who invented the whole notion of education.

cue0021403
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Now, in answer to your question, we had a whole tribe.

cue0021404
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:31.000
In antiquity, we had one tribe whose sole purpose to exist was to educate.

cue0021405
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.000
And that was the Shevet Levi.

cue0021406
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Yeru Mishpatecha Le'aakov V'toratecha Le'Yiśraʾel.

cue0021407
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
They were the teachers.

cue0021408
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
They were the descendants of the tribe of Moshe Rabbenu.

cue0021409
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:50.000
And therefore, all the matters of education, as long as the temple was intact, was in their hands.

cue0021410
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.000
In addition, so we had teachers.

cue0021411
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:01.000
And we had teachers that were in charge of transmitting the Tora.

cue0021412
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
I want to come to a few more points.

cue0021413
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Furthermore, the Tora says many times,

cue0021414
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Ve'gatah le'bincha, teach your children,

cue0021415
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.000
v'shinan tam le'vanecha, v'tvartavah.

cue0021416
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.000
In the Shemaʿ, it says that.

cue0021417
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
And that's why we repeat it.

cue0021418
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.000
We say the Shemaʿ because it's important, because we have to teach, transmit the thing to the children.

cue0021419
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
But, here comes the most important thing.

cue0021420
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:30.000
There's a whole book, the book of Proverbs, which is devoted to educate.

cue0021421
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Either to educate in the family, within the bosom of the family, or within the bosom of the school.

cue0021422
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.000
So therefore, we have, we do have education is central in Judaism.

cue0021423
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.000
In the Tora, it mentions it a few times, more than a few times.

cue0021424
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Kish alechavimcha, mahalimor mazod, v'amartalahem.

cue0021425
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
So always, the Tora says.

cue0021426
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:58.000
But, and there's one book, the book of Proverbs, which is dedicated to education.

cue0021427
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.000
I'm sorry.

cue0021428
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
That's the answer.

cue0021429
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Now, ready to, we're ready to study.

cue0021430
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Alright.

cue0021431
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:18.000
We're going to study the parasha, this three last parashiot,

cue0021432
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.000
with which we end with the book of Exodus, of Shemot.

cue0021433
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.000
They deal with one single subject.

cue0021434
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.000
The building of the Mishkan.

cue0021435
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Alright.

cue0021436
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Now, you have three parashiot.

cue0021437
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Three parashiot.

cue0021438
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000
No, I'm sorry, four parashiot.

cue0021439
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Five, I'm sorry, I'm making a mistake here.

cue0021440
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:53.000
Teruma, Tesaveh, Kittisa, Vayakhel, Pekudim.

cue0021441
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Five parashiot.

cue0021442
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Dealing with one central subject.

cue0021443
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
The building of the Mishkan.

cue0021444
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Now, and that's the way the book of Exodus ends.

cue0021445
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.000
The book of Exodus ends with the, when the Jewish people actually build the Mishkan.

cue0021446
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Alright.

cue0021447
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.000
I explained everything.

cue0021448
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Then we are going to give an introduction, because most people do not understand.

cue0021449
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.000
It's a very difficult topic.

cue0021450
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.000
But let me explain a few things before.

cue0021451
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.000
The relationship between the beginning and the end of the book of Exodus.

cue0021452
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:40.000
At the beginning of the book of Exodus, we find a people, the children of Israel,

cue0021453
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
who are at the bottom of society.

cue0021454
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.000
They are slaves.

cue0021455
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Alright.

cue0021456
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.000
They have no rights.

cue0021457
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.000
They have no education.

cue0021458
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.000
They have nothing.

cue0021459
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.000
They have no spiritual life.

cue0021460
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
As the Ḥakhamim say,

cue0021461
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.000
We were idol worshippers.

cue0021462
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
We say it in the Gadar.

cue0021463
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.000
They were also idol worshippers, our ancestors in Egypt.

cue0021464
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.000
That is true.

cue0021465
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.000
So we are at the bottom of the society.

cue0021466
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.000
At the end of the book of Exodus,

cue0021467
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.000
we are at the top.

cue0021468
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.000
In the sense, something which is baffles the imagination.

cue0021469
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:33.000
God chooses to dwell among us, with the Jewish people.

cue0021470
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:39.000
The word Mishkan, from which two other words derive, I'll tell you in a minute.

cue0021471
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.000
One means Shachan, to dwell.

cue0021472
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
And the other word Shekhina.

cue0021473
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Shekhina means the dwelling of God.

cue0021474
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Now, God chooses to dwell in the Mishkan.

cue0021475
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
What does it mean?

cue0021476
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
It means like this.

cue0021477
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Suppose I ask you,

cue0021478
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.000
I mean, within the scheme of the Tora,

cue0021479
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.000
What is the highest point of the universe?

cue0021480
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.000
So you would say, the highest point of the universe is the Shamaim,

cue0021481
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.000
where the Malachim are,

cue0021482
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.000
the throne of God.

cue0021483
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.000
That's what you say.

cue0021484
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Of course, when you say that, you know, Malachim, angels, heavens.

cue0021485
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Here, the Tora has a revolutionary idea.

cue0021486
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.000
It says no.

cue0021487
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.000
The highest point of the universe,

cue0021488
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.000
is where God dwells.

cue0021489
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
And the dwelling place of God,

cue0021490
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
is not in heavens,

cue0021491
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.000
is on earth.

cue0021492
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.000
This is a revolutionary idea.

cue0021493
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Means, in a sense,

cue0021494
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.000
that the Malachim have to pray to God,

cue0021495
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.000
who is in the Aris.

cue0021496
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
You know, I mean, this, you have to inverse,

cue0021497
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
through the whole notion of the Mishkan,

cue0021498
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.000
the relationship,

cue0021499
00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.000
the whole structure of the universe is inversed.

cue0021500
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.000
In other words, if God is Shekhin,

cue0021501
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.000
as we are going to say here, in the Mishkan,

cue0021502
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:12.000
means therefore, that the angels, they have to look up to whom?

cue0021503
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.000
To God. Where is God?

cue0021504
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
On earth.

cue0021505
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.000
No.

cue0021506
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.000
This, no.

cue0021507
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.000
This is the notion of the Mishkan.

cue0021508
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.000
The Mishkan means, that from now on,

cue0021509
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.000
God, in a sense, switches addresses.

cue0021510
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
The address of God is changed.

cue0021511
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.000
He changes addresses.

cue0021512
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.000
In what way He changes addresses?

cue0021513
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.000
He is no longer Shekhin,

cue0021514
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.000
but Meromim.

cue0021515
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.000
But Mishkan, means He is Shekhin here in the Aris.

cue0021516
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.000
V'shakhanti v'tokham.

cue0021517
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
That's what it says.

cue0021518
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.000
It's extraordinary. The pasuq says,

cue0021519
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.000
V'asuli Mishkan.

cue0021520
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.000
They should build for me a Mishkan, a tent.

cue0021521
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.000
V'shakhanti.

cue0021522
00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.000
And my permanent address

cue0021523
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.000
would be with them.

cue0021524
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
But do you take it literally, or maybe it's something else?

cue0021525
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.000
I mean, as literal as it could be.

cue0021526
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
This is the whole notion of the Mishkan.

cue0021527
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
The whole notion of the V'tamikdash,

cue0021528
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.000
that the Jewish people have,

cue0021529
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.000
is to inverse

cue0021530
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Shamayim to Aris.

cue0021531
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.000
The highest point of the universe,

cue0021532
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
therefore, is this earth.

cue0021533
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Why?

cue0021534
00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.000
If you are, I don't know, in the middle of the universe,

cue0021535
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.000
where would you face up to?

cue0021536
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.000
To where God is, correct?

cue0021537
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Where God is.

cue0021538
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.000
Here on the earth.

cue0021539
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.000
This is the idea of the Mishkan.

cue0021540
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Now you understand the idea of the Mishkan, right?

cue0021541
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.000
And there's a simple theory behind it.

cue0021542
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.000
Simple theory behind it.

cue0021543
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Rightly or wrongly.

cue0021544
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
The simple theory is this.

cue0021545
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.000
Out of all those celestial beings,

cue0021546
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.000
who may be intellectually superior to us,

cue0021547
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.000
may be more powerful, more intelligent, and so on,

cue0021548
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.000
there's a difference.

cue0021549
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Those beings are so great,

cue0021550
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.000
that they have no freedom of choice.

cue0021551
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.000
They cannot choose.

cue0021552
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
They are what they are.

cue0021553
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.000
We, humans,

cue0021554
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.000
we are unique,

cue0021555
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.000
because we could choose.

cue0021556
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
And therefore, in a sense,

cue0021557
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.000
we are the one who holds the balance of power

cue0021558
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.000
in the universe.

cue0021559
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.000
If the universe is good or bad,

cue0021560
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.000
it doesn't depend up to the angels.

cue0021561
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.000
The angels are what they are.

cue0021562
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.000
It depends up to us.

cue0021563
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.000
And therefore, the notion of the Mishkan,

cue0021564
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.000
I want you to understand,

cue0021565
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.000
which is a revolutionary idea,

cue0021566
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.000
within the concept of the history of

cue0021567
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
ideas of religion, of religion,

cue0021568
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.000
this is a revolutionary idea.

cue0021569
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.000
God dwells here.

cue0021570
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.000
V'shachanti v'tocham.

cue0021571
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Right?

cue0021572
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.000
And therefore,

cue0021573
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.000
that's why we understand why

cue0021574
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.000
the last five perashiyot,

cue0021575
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.000
the Tora devotes five perashiyot,

cue0021576
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.000
five perashiyot,

cue0021577
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.000
to the idea of the Mishkan.

cue0021578
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.000
This idea of the Mishkan

cue0021579
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.000
is going to be later on

cue0021580
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
translated

cue0021581
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.000
into the Temple

cue0021582
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.000
by King Solomon.

cue0021583
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
Alright?

cue0021584
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.000
The Temple of King Solomon

cue0021585
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.000
means the same thing.

cue0021586
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.000
Yes?

cue0021587
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.000
We're going to see it.

cue0021588
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.000
We're going to study it.

cue0021589
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.000
That God dwells not in Heaven.

cue0021590
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.000
If the people in Heaven

cue0021591
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
want something from God,

cue0021592
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.000
they have to look up to it.

cue0021593
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Did you say that there is no Beta miqdash?

cue0021594
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Oh!

cue0021595
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.000
Now that there is no Beta miqdash,

cue0021596
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.000
the qabbala has a beautiful idea.

cue0021597
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.000
The qabbala,

cue0021598
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.000
people don't understand.

cue0021599
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.000
The qabbala,

cue0021600
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.000
people think the qabbala is

cue0021601
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.000
hum hum,

cue0021602
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.000
shaking.

cue0021603
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.000
qabbala,

cue0021604
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
it has some very profound ideas.

cue0021605
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.000
Very beautiful ideas.

cue0021606
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.000
qabbala says like this.

cue0021607
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.000
Now that the Beta miqdash is destroyed,

cue0021608
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.000
God is in Galut.

cue0021609
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Let's think about that.

cue0021610
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.000
He's in exile, God.

cue0021611
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.000
That's what the qabbala says.

cue0021612
00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.000
Very beautiful idea.

cue0021613
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Let me explain to you

cue0021614
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.000
what it means.

cue0021615
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.000
It means like this.

cue0021616
00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.000
The real dwelling of God

cue0021617
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.000
is here.

cue0021618
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.000
Now He was kicked out,

cue0021619
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.000
so to speak,

cue0021620
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.000
from His permanent dwelling.

cue0021621
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.000
That's why He's in Heaven.

cue0021622
00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.000
But while He's in Heaven,

cue0021623
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.000
that is Galut for God.

cue0021624
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.000
Because the Shekhina of God,

cue0021625
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
He wants to be here.

cue0021626
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.000
He wants to be among us.

cue0021627
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.000
He chose

cue0021628
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.000
this humanoid race,

cue0021629
