00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:05.000
Let me explain to you.

cue0022159
00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:09.000
You have a throne.

cue0022160
00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:12.000
And under the throne

cue0022161
00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.000
you have a little bit like a cushion.

cue0022162
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:18.000
So to speak,

cue0022163
00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:21.000
HaShamaim Kis'o

cue0022164
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.000
That's the way Yishai Yareth says it.

cue0022165
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:26.000
The throne goes up to heaven.

cue0022166
00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:29.000
Ha'ares Hadom Raglad

cue0022167
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:31.000
And in the earth,

cue0022168
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.000
which is in the Beta miqdash,

cue0022169
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.000
is the footstool.

cue0022170
00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:35.000
You see?

cue0022171
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.000
So therefore,

cue0022172
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:39.000
the Eidut is like the link

cue0022173
00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:43.000
between God,

cue0022174
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.000
the highest form expression of God,

cue0022175
00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.000
and the tablets.

cue0022176
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.000
Alright?

cue0022177
00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.000
So it's called Mishkan Eidut

cue0022178
00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
because there you have the tablets,

cue0022179
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:57.000
the covenant made between God and Israel

cue0022180
00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.000
in Mount Sinai.

cue0022181
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:00.000
It is the document.

cue0022182
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
It is a document.

cue0022183
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:02.000
So to speak,

cue0022184
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:04.000
signed by God.

cue0022185
00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:05.000
And establishing.

cue0022186
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.000
And that's the Tora.

cue0022187
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:07.000
The Eidut.

cue0022188
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.000
Alright?

cue0022189
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Now,

cue0022190
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.000
this represents,

cue0022191
00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:12.000
I don't know if you remember,

cue0022192
00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:16.000
when we were in Sinai,

cue0022193
00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:17.000
there was a group,

cue0022194
00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:18.000
ʾAharon,

cue0022195
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.000
and Moshe,

cue0022196
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Nadav,

cue0022197
00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:21.000
Abihu,

cue0022198
00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:22.000
they went all the way to the top.

cue0022199
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.000
Moshe Rabbenu made it,

cue0022200
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.000
was the only one who made it,

cue0022201
00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:25.000
all the way to the top.

cue0022202
00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:28.000
Then to the middle of the mountain,

cue0022203
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:32.000
there were the Shibaim Zekanim.

cue0022204
00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
The elder statements.

cue0022205
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Who were the elder statements?

cue0022206
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:40.000
They were the legal representative

cue0022207
00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:43.000
of Israel.

cue0022208
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:47.000
We were represented by 70 statements.

cue0022209
00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:48.000
In other words,

cue0022210
00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:51.000
they are our legal representative.

cue0022211
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:53.000
They were the members of the Sanhedrin,

cue0022212
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:56.000
they were the people who interpreted the law,

cue0022213
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
and the people who executed the law.

cue0022214
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:00.000
Alright?

cue0022215
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.000
That's why,

cue0022216
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:07.000
this Eidut represents the second stage.

cue0022217
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:08.000
And these are,

cue0022218
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.000
we also have,

cue0022219
00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:10.000
we have Kohanim,

cue0022220
00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
then we have Lebiim.

cue0022221
00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:15.000
The Lebiim who are the one who teach the Tora.

cue0022222
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.000
You understand what I'm saying?

cue0022223
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
So therefore you have the Mishkan.

cue0022224
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.000
It's called one Mishkan

cue0022225
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
because it is the place where God lives.

cue0022226
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
Mishkan Eidut,

cue0022227
00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:25.000
because it's the tablets,

cue0022228
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.000
the testimony,

cue0022229
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
the covenant,

cue0022230
00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:29.000
the document,

cue0022231
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:31.000
written and signed by God,

cue0022232
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.000
and Israel, so to speak,

cue0022233
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:35.000
that is the document.

cue0022234
00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:37.000
And this represents the legal apparatus

cue0022235
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
of the Jewish people.

cue0022236
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.000
When we were in Sinai,

cue0022237
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.000
there were the Zekanim

cue0022238
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.000
in the middle of the mountain.

cue0022239
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.000
Alright?

cue0022240
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:45.000
And then you have,

cue0022241
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:46.000
in the Metavigdash,

cue0022242
00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:49.000
you have something which is called Qodesh.

cue0022243
00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.000
You have Qodesh HaKorashim,

cue0022244
00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.000
which is the highest,

cue0022245
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.000
then you have the Qodesh.

cue0022246
00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.000
The Qodesh is the place

cue0022247
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.000
where is the altar,

cue0022248
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.000
and when you bring the Korbanot,

cue0022249
00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.000
service to God.

cue0022250
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:01.000
And then there is,

cue0022251
00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:02.000
is another way

cue0022252
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.000
in which the Mishkan is called,

cue0022253
00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:07.000
is called Ohel HaEidut.

cue0022254
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.000
No longer Mishkan,

cue0022255
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:11.000
because Mishkan is the residence of God,

cue0022256
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.000
but Ohel, a tent,

cue0022257
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:17.000
where the people assemble

cue0022258
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:20.000
to discuss

cue0022259
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:23.000
whatever national crisis happens to be.

cue0022260
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.000
When there was a national crisis

cue0022261
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
among the Jewish people,

cue0022262
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.000
the Jewish people met

cue0022263
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:32.000
in Ohel HaEidut,

cue0022264
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:35.000
in the tent,

cue0022265
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:36.000
like in the Knesset,

cue0022266
00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.000
like to the Knesset,

cue0022267
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
but that was made by the people.

cue0022268
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.000
That was the people,

cue0022269
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:41.000
that was mostly like a,

cue0022270
00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:43.000
like an assembly hall in America,

cue0022271
00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:45.000
in which the whole town,

cue0022272
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
like a town meeting hall.

cue0022273
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
And therefore, the ʾohel moʿed

cue0022274
00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:51.000
is the Ohel in which moʿed,

cue0022275
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:52.000
in the sense,

cue0022276
00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
B'twa'adu.

cue0022277
00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:55.000
You see, you understand Arabic?

cue0022278
00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.000
B'twa'adu, there,

cue0022279
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:58.000
means where they convey,

cue0022280
00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:59.000
they meet.

cue0022281
00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:00.000
B'twa'adu, that's the word.

cue0022282
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.000
ʾohel moʿed, literally means

cue0022283
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:05.000
the place in which the Jewish people

cue0022284
00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:08.000
B'twa'adu, they congregate.

cue0022285
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.000
That would be the word in English.

cue0022286
00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:11.000
They congregate there.

cue0022287
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:14.000
And that represents

cue0022288
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:15.000
the rest of the people

cue0022289
00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:19.000
at the foot of Mount Sinai.

cue0022290
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.000
You see, there were three,

cue0022291
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.000
there were two people on the top,

cue0022292
00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.000
people in the middle,

cue0022293
00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.000
people at the bottom.

cue0022294
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:26.000
And this also,

cue0022295
00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:28.000
you have another equivalent like this

cue0022296
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:30.000
in the Mishkan,

cue0022297
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.000
which is the Haser,

cue0022298
00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
the courtyard in the Mishkan,

cue0022299
00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.000
in which every Jew,

cue0022300
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
man and woman,

cue0022301
00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.000
were permitted to enter.

cue0022302
00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:42.000
And the same thing you have

cue0022303
00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:43.000
in the Bet hammiqdash,

cue0022304
00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.000
you had the Qodesh HaKorashim,

cue0022305
00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:47.000
you had the Qodesh,

cue0022306
00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.000
and then you have HaAzara.

cue0022307
00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:52.000
HaAzara is where everybody,

cue0022308
00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:53.000
men and women,

cue0022309
00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:56.000
are permitted to enter there.

cue0022310
00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Alright?

cue0022311
00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:58.000
Yes, Maurice.

cue0022312
00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:00.000
Ohel, Ha'adu, and ʾohel moʿed,

cue0022313
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.000
the same thing?

cue0022314
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Yes.

cue0022315
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:03.000
Ohel, the same thing,

cue0022316
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:06.000
is the place where the people congregate.

cue0022317
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.000
But it's interesting,

cue0022318
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:10.000
there it's no longer called a Mishkan.

cue0022319
00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:11.000
You see?

cue0022320
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:13.000
It's called an Ohel.

cue0022321
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:16.000
Because Mishkan is vis-a-vis God.

cue0022322
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
Although it's the same place,

cue0022323
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
it's the same spot,

cue0022324
00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:22.000
you know,

cue0022325
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.000
but the name varies.

cue0022326
00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:25.000
So they call it this.

cue0022327
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:29.000
I want you to know this thing.

cue0022328
00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:30.000
Alright?

cue0022329
00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.000
Now.

cue0022330
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.000
Alright.

cue0022331
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:38.000
Yes.

cue0022332
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:42.000
No.

cue0022333
00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:43.000
No.

cue0022334
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.000
Later on,

cue0022335
00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:45.000
Sareeha.

cue0022336
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:46.000
No and yes.

cue0022337
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:47.000
I'm sorry.

cue0022338
00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:48.000
Yes.

cue0022339
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:49.000
Very important.

cue0022340
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.000
First of all,

cue0022341
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:51.000
that's a very important thing.

cue0022342
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:54.000
At the end of the 40 years,

cue0022343
00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:57.000
because Moshe Rabbenu wrote the Tora

cue0022344
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:00.000
at the end of 40 years in the desert.

cue0022345
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.000
When he writes the Tora,

cue0022346
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:06.000
he writes 13 copies of the Tora,

cue0022347
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:08.000
Moshe Rabbenu.

cue0022348
00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:10.000
And the way it goes is as follows.

cue0022349
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:15.000
It gives one copy of the Sepher Tora

cue0022350
00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.000
to each tribe.

cue0022351
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:20.000
And one copy,

cue0022352
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:24.000
he puts in the Aron Ha'idut.

cue0022353
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:26.000
In that Aron Ha'idut,

cue0022354
00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.000
he leaves it there.

cue0022355
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.000
You see?

cue0022356
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.000
And therefore,

cue0022357
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.000
why this is so important?

cue0022358
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Why this?

cue0022359
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:33.000
Because like this.

cue0022360
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:34.000
Suppose, I don't know,

cue0022361
00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:37.000
a thousand years later,

cue0022362
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:41.000
U'bevo Moshe la'Qodesh.

cue0022363
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:42.000
So, I say,

cue0022364
00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:46.000
it has to be with a Bab.

cue0022365
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.000
No, it doesn't have to be with a Bab.

cue0022366
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:52.000
How do you know how to write it?

cue0022367
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:56.000
There's only one way how do you do it.

cue0022368
00:34:56.000 --> 00:35:00.000
You go to the Bet hammiqdash,

cue0022369
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:03.000
and then you check it

cue0022370
00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.000
against the original.

cue0022371
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.000
That is the original.

cue0022372
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:06.000
And therefore,

cue0022373
00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:09.000
this original serves to validate

cue0022374
00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.000
all future copies.

cue0022375
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:13.000
Do you understand?

cue0022376
00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:14.000
Ultimately,

cue0022377
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:16.000
sometimes there's a voice with a Bab.

cue0022378
00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:18.000
Sometimes it's without a Bab.

cue0022379
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:21.000
You could argue with me,

cue0022380
00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:22.000
I could argue with Bab.

cue0022381
00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:24.000
How could we prove it?

cue0022382
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:25.000
Ultimately,

cue0022383
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.000
there's only one way to do it.

cue0022384
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.000
We validate.

cue0022385
00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:30.000
Now, out of this

cue0022386
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.000
came a very important Sepharadi custom.

cue0022387
00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:33.000
You will not believe it,

cue0022388
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.000
but only the Sepharadim have discussed it.

cue0022389
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:36.000
Not only Sepharadim,

cue0022390
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.000
also Temanim.

cue0022391
00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.000
Sepharadim and Oriental Jews in the Orient,

cue0022392
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.000
like the Yemenites,

cue0022393
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:42.000
they have it.

cue0022394
00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.000
We had,

cue0022395
00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:44.000
for instance,

cue0022396
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Halab was famous for this.

cue0022397
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.000
Sham also was famous for this.

cue0022398
00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
Egypt was famous for this.

cue0022399
00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:51.000
Each community had a Taj.

cue0022400
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:54.000
You know what Taj is?

cue0022401
00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
The word Taj means a crown.

cue0022402
00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
But it was not a crown.

cue0022403
00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:02.000
It was a manuscript Sepher Tora.

cue0022404
00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:05.000
The oldest and most authoritative things

cue0022405
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:07.000
that was kept

cue0022406
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.000
in the archives of the community.

cue0022407
00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:12.000
And therefore,

cue0022408
00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:14.000
whenever there's a problem in the Sepher Tora,

cue0022409
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:15.000
it should be written this way,

cue0022410
00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.000
not should be written this way.

cue0022411
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.000
They used to go

cue0022412
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.000
and check it

cue0022413
00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:24.000
against this Taj.

cue0022414
00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:25.000
You understand?

cue0022415
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:27.000
And thereby they determine

cue0022416
00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:30.000
whether it is a kosher or unkosher Sepher Tora.

cue0022417
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
Every single Sepharadi community

cue0022418
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.000
throughout history

cue0022419
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
up to the modern times,

cue0022420
00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:40.000
the most famous Taj of all

cue0022421
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:42.000
is the Taj of Aramsoba,

cue0022422
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:43.000
of Halab.

cue0022423
00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.000
Why?

cue0022424
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:48.000
Because it belonged to Rambam.

cue0022425
00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:50.000
And what happened to it,

cue0022426
00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:55.000
part of it was burnt or destroyed.

cue0022427
